# The repo is public, so anything secret that lands here is published the
# moment it is committed. These entries exist to make that mistake impossible
# rather than merely unlikely — every credential Criba uses is read from
# process.env and belongs in the Vercel dashboard, never in a file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules/
.vercel/
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Service-account keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*-credentials.json
service-account*.json
